{"v":15,"id":"e05","kid":"emma","title":"The Water Cycle","zh":"水的循环","level":"B1","genre":"科学","src":"facts","sum":"水在地球上不停地循环：蒸发、凝结成云、降水，再流回大海或渗入地下。能直接使用的淡水很少，所以要节约用水。","words":286,"paras":[{"t":"The water you drink today may be millions of years old. A dinosaur might once have drunk it! This is possible because Earth's water moves in a never-ending circle called the water cycle.","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,9,"water",-1],[10,13,"you",-1],[14,19,"drink",-1],[20,25,"today",-1],[26,29,"may",-1],[30,32,"be",-1],[33,41,"millions",-1],[42,44,"of",-1],[45,50,"years",-1],[51,54,"old",-1],[56,57,"a",-1],[58,66,"dinosaur",-1],[67,72,"might",-1],[73,77,"once",-1],[78,82,"have",-1],[83,88,"drunk",-1],[89,91,"it",-1],[93,97,"this",-1],[98,100,"is",-1],[101,109,"possible",-1],[110,117,"because",-1],[118,125,"Earth's",-1],[126,131,"water",-1],[132,137,"moves",-1],[138,140,"in",-1],[141,142,"a",-1],[143,155,"never-ending",-1],[156,162,"circle",-1],[163,169,"called",-1],[170,173,"the",-1],[174,179,"water",0],[180,185,"cycle",0]]},{"t":"The cycle has no real beginning or end, but let's start with the ocean. When the sun heats the water in oceans, lakes and rivers, some of it turns into an invisible gas called water vapor. This is called evaporation. Plants also give off water vapor through their leaves. The warm, wet air rises into the sky.","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,9,"cycle",-1],[10,13,"has",-1],[14,16,"no",-1],[17,21,"real",-1],[22,31,"beginning",-1],[32,34,"or",-1],[35,38,"end",-1],[40,43,"but",-1],[44,49,"let's",-1],[50,55,"start",-1],[56,60,"with",-1],[61,64,"the",-1],[65,70,"ocean",-1],[72,76,"when",-1],[77,80,"the",-1],[81,84,"sun",-1],[85,90,"heats",-1],[91,94,"the",-1],[95,100,"water",-1],[101,103,"in",-1],[104,110,"oceans",-1],[112,117,"lakes",-1],[118,121,"and",-1],[122,128,"rivers",-1],[130,134,"some",-1],[135,137,"of",-1],[138,140,"it",-1],[141,146,"turns",3],[147,151,"into",3],[152,154,"an",-1],[155,164,"invisible",-1],[165,168,"gas",-1],[169,175,"called",-1],[176,181,"water",1],[182,187,"vapor",1],[189,193,"this",-1],[194,196,"is",-1],[197,203,"called",-1],[204,215,"evaporation",-1],[217,223,"plants",-1],[224,228,"also",-1],[229,233,"give",2],[234,237,"off",2],[238,243,"water",1],[244,249,"vapor",1],[250,257,"through",-1],[258,263,"their",-1],[264,270,"leaves",-1],[272,275,"the",-1],[276,280,"warm",-1],[282,285,"wet",-1],[286,289,"air",-1],[290,295,"rises",-1],[296,300,"into",-1],[301,304,"the",-1],[305,308,"sky",-1]]},{"t":"High above the ground, the air is much colder. There, the water vapor cools down and turns back into tiny drops of water. This is called condensation. Billions of these tiny drops come together to form clouds. You can see condensation at home, too: think of the drops of water on the outside of a cold glass of juice on a hot day.","w":[[0,4,"high",-1],[5,10,"above",-1],[11,14,"the",-1],[15,21,"ground",-1],[23,26,"the",-1],[27,30,"air",-1],[31,33,"is",-1],[34,38,"much",-1],[39,45,"colder",-1],[47,52,"there",-1],[54,57,"the",-1],[58,63,"water",1],[64,69,"vapor",1],[70,75,"cools",5],[76,80,"down",5],[81,84,"and",-1],[85,90,"turns",4],[91,95,"back",4],[96,100,"into",4],[101,105,"tiny",-1],[106,111,"drops",-1],[112,114,"of",-1],[115,120,"water",-1],[122,126,"this",-1],[127,129,"is",-1],[130,136,"called",-1],[137,149,"condensation",-1],[151,159,"billions",-1],[160,162,"of",-1],[163,168,"these",-1],[169,173,"tiny",-1],[174,179,"drops",-1],[180,184,"come",6],[185,193,"together",6],[194,196,"to",-1],[197,201,"form",-1],[202,208,"clouds",-1],[210,213,"you",-1],[214,217,"can",-1],[218,221,"see",-1],[222,234,"condensation",-1],[235,237,"at",-1],[238,242,"home",-1],[244,247,"too",-1],[249,254,"think",7],[255,257,"of",7],[258,261,"the",-1],[262,267,"drops",-1],[268,270,"of",-1],[271,276,"water",-1],[277,279,"on",-1],[280,283,"the",-1],[284,291,"outside",-1],[292,294,"of",-1],[295,296,"a",-1],[297,301,"cold",-1],[302,307,"glass",-1],[308,310,"of",-1],[311,316,"juice",-1],[317,319,"on",-1],[320,321,"a",-1],[322,325,"hot",-1],[326,329,"day",-1]]},{"t":"As more and more drops join together, they become heavy. When they are too heavy to stay in the air, they fall to the ground as rain. If the air is very cold, they fall as snow or hail.","w":[[0,2,"as",-1],[3,7,"more",8],[8,11,"and",8],[12,16,"more",8],[17,22,"drops",-1],[23,27,"join",9],[28,36,"together",9],[38,42,"they",-1],[43,49,"become",-1],[50,55,"heavy",-1],[57,61,"when",-1],[62,66,"they",-1],[67,70,"are",-1],[71,74,"too",-1],[75,80,"heavy",-1],[81,83,"to",-1],[84,88,"stay",-1],[89,91,"in",-1],[92,95,"the",-1],[96,99,"air",-1],[101,105,"they",-1],[106,110,"fall",-1],[111,113,"to",-1],[114,117,"the",-1],[118,124,"ground",-1],[125,127,"as",-1],[128,132,"rain",-1],[134,136,"if",-1],[137,140,"the",-1],[141,144,"air",-1],[145,147,"is",-1],[148,152,"very",-1],[153,157,"cold",-1],[159,163,"they",-1],[164,168,"fall",-1],[169,171,"as",-1],[172,176,"snow",-1],[177,179,"or",-1],[180,184,"hail",-1]]},{"t":"Some of the water runs into rivers and flows back to the sea. Some soaks into the ground and becomes groundwater, which can stay underground for a very long time. Some is frozen in ice and snow on high mountains. Sooner or later, the sun warms it again, and the cycle continues.","w":[[0,4,"some",-1],[5,7,"of",-1],[8,11,"the",-1],[12,17,"water",-1],[18,22,"runs",-1],[23,27,"into",-1],[28,34,"rivers",-1],[35,38,"and",-1],[39,44,"flows",-1],[45,49,"back",-1],[50,52,"to",-1],[53,56,"the",-1],[57,60,"sea",-1],[62,66,"some",-1],[67,72,"soaks",10],[73,77,"into",10],[78,81,"the",-1],[82,88,"ground",-1],[89,92,"and",-1],[93,100,"becomes",-1],[101,112,"groundwater",-1],[114,119,"which",-1],[120,123,"can",-1],[124,128,"stay",-1],[129,140,"underground",-1],[141,144,"for",-1],[145,146,"a",-1],[147,151,"very",-1],[152,156,"long",-1],[157,161,"time",-1],[163,167,"some",-1],[168,170,"is",-1],[171,177,"frozen",-1],[178,180,"in",-1],[181,184,"ice",-1],[185,188,"and",-1],[189,193,"snow",-1],[194,196,"on",-1],[197,201,"high",-1],[202,211,"mountains",-1],[213,219,"so